	I have a full screen editor written in C that I have released
to the public domain.  I have spent 6 years on this editor, so it is a
very mature product.  For those of you who hate modeless editors like
emacs, it may be the answer.  It is somewhat like vi (insert/command mode),
and has a totally user customizable command set.  Right now, versions
exits for IBM-PC's, Unix (4.2 BSD), and the atari 520ST.  It is easily
ported to any machine with a C complier.
	This is a mature product with a full user manual, and all the 
portability glitches isolated and identified.  If you are interested,
please send mail back to me directly.  If I get enought replies, I will
post the entire source.  Otherwise, I will send to you directly.  If
you want a copy of the IBM-PC version, send a floppy disk to
me directly, and I will send it back to you.
